From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [engine] build: pin -faltivec-src-compat=mixed for ppc64

clang decides how AltiVec/VSX vector code is typed with
-faltivec-src-compat: whether a vector compare yields a vector mask or a
scalar, and how a scalar converts to a vector. Its default is "mixed",
and clang's -Wdeprecated-altivec-src-compat warning (188 of them in
Skia, engine track REPORT.md section 8.4) says the default will become
"xl". Measured with clang 22.1.8 on ppc64le, 2026-11-19:

  mode     probe: (int4)(a < b),           skcms_TransformBaseline.cc
           a={1,2,3,4} b={2,2,2,2}         (Skia, the portable path)
  mixed    {-1,0,0,0}  correct             compiles (17 warnings)
  gcc      {-1,0,0,0}  correct             2 errors: invalid conversion
                                           between vector types
  xl       {0,0,0,0}   silently scalar     5 errors: static_assert
                                           sizeof(bool) == sizeof(v)

So the only mode in which this tree both compiles and computes vector
masks is today's default. Pin it, so that the day clang flips its default
the build either keeps today's semantics or, where code needs another
mode, fails here rather than in a pixel. The engine track's suggestion to
pin "gcc" does not compile skcms.

It is a GN arg so a by-hand build can show that the pin is what holds:
ppc64_altivec_src_compat="" leaves the compiler default. The
flutter-engine recipe asserts that -faltivec-src-compat=mixed reaches
every ppc64 compile and that no other mode appears anywhere.

Class: upstreamable fix (a portability guard: pins the vector semantics
the code is written for; no effect while clang's default stays mixed).
---
 engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -47,6 +47,14 @@
   # 2.07). GN ignores $CFLAGS, so a distro's ISA policy has to come in here.
   ppc64_cpu = ""
 
+  # ppc64: clang's -faltivec-src-compat mode, pinned to "mixed", today's
+  # default and the only mode in which Skia's skcms both compiles and gets
+  # vector masks from vector compares ("gcc" and "xl" fail to compile
+  # skcms; "xl" also turns vector compares scalar). clang says its default
+  # will change to "xl". Empty leaves the compiler default (for testing
+  # that the pin is what holds).
+  ppc64_altivec_src_compat = "mixed"
+
   # Turn compiler warnings into errors. Builds with a compiler other than the
   # pinned prebuilt clang (e.g. a distro's system clang, which is newer or
   # older and has a different warning set) set this to false.
@@ -424,6 +432,9 @@
           "-mtune=$ppc64_cpu",
         ]
       }
+      if (is_clang && ppc64_altivec_src_compat != "") {
+        cflags += [ "-faltivec-src-compat=$ppc64_altivec_src_compat" ]
+      }
     }
   }
 
